  "Solution": "20 is \\(25\\%\\) of 80. The calculation here gives 25.\n\nAlternative method 1: Compute the decimal quotient, then multiply by 100\n\nMultiplication and division have equal priority, so evaluate from left to right. First \\(20\\div80=0.25\\). Multiplying by \\(100\\) moves the decimal point two places to the right, so\n\\[\n20\\div80\\times100=0.25\\times100=25.\n\\]",
